The rules that call odoc know that it is going to read the ODOC_SYNTAX
variable, and can rebuild as needed.

  $ cat > dune-project << EOF
  > (lang dune 1.1)
  > (package (name l))
  > EOF

  $ cat > dune << EOF
  > (library
  >  (public_name l))
  > EOF

  $ cat > l.ml << EOF
  > module type X = sig end
  > EOF

  $ detect () {
  > if grep -q '>sig<' $1 ; then
  >   echo it is ocaml
  > elif grep -q '{ ... }' $1 ; then
  >   echo it is reason
  > else
  >   echo it is unknown
  > fi
  > }

